---
/*
  Where Kit sends a reader the moment they submit the form.

  Set on the Kit form, 2 Sep: "Redirect to an external page" pointing here.
  Before that, Kit showed its own bare success message on app.kit.com, so
  somebody who signed up on denvillee.com was handed off to a page with none
  of his site on it.

  The heading used to read "You are in", which was not true yet: the list is
  double opt-in, so nobody is in until they click the link in the email. This
  page's whole job is to make that second step obvious enough that people
  actually take it, because an unconfirmed subscriber is the same as no
  subscriber.
*/
import Shell from '../../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Mark from '../../components/marks/Mark.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
---
<Shell title={`One more step · ${site.name}`} description="Confirm your email." noindex={true}>
  <section class="band shell sub-step">
    <p class="sub-step-k">Almost there</p>
    <h1 class="sub-step-h is-display">
      Check your inbox to <span class="u">confirm<Mark kind="underline" color="blue" draw={true} /></span><span class="dot">.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="sub-step-d">
      There is an email on its way from Denvil Lee. Open it and click the
      confirm link, and you are on the list.
    </p>
    <p class="sub-step-n">
      If it is not there in a few minutes, look in promotions or spam. Marking
      it as not spam helps the next one land where you can see it.
    </p>
    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/">Back home</a></p>
  </section>
</Shell>
